boot, on every filter reload and on interface events. A shell script that
adds routes, gateways or interfaces behind its back holds only until the
next re-apply: the change is silently reverted - or worse, half survives,
and the GUI now disagrees with the kernel (ghost routes, duplicate gateways,
states that never clear, and an XML restore that wipes it all). Routing and
interfaces MUST therefore be created in the GUI, where they are also cleanly
undone. The only script here, verify.sh, is strictly read-only.

All values below come from @CONFFILE@ in this bundle. The private key is
NEVER written in these instructions - take it from the PrivateKey line in
the [Interface] section of the conf file, and paste it only into the one
Private Key field named below.

A. Package
 1. System > Package Manager > Available Packages: install "WireGuard".
B. Tunnel
 2. VPN > WireGuard > Tunnels > Add Tunnel.
 3. Enable; Description: @BASE@. Listen Port: leave default (client role).
    Interface Keys: paste the PrivateKey value FROM THE CONF FILE - the
    public key derives automatically. Save Tunnel.
C. Peer (the EDT1 server)
 4. VPN > WireGuard > Peers > Add Peer. Tunnel: tun_wg0 (@BASE@).
 5. Dynamic Endpoint: unchecked. Endpoint: @ENDPOINT_HOST@  Port:
    @ENDPOINT_PORT@ (this is the PUBLIC port the server is reached on -
    keep it).
 6. Public Key: @SERVER_PUBKEY@
 7. Keep Alive: @KEEPALIVE@. Allowed IPs: @ALLOWED@
    Save Peer, then Apply Changes.
D. Interface assignment
 8. Interfaces > Assignments: select the new tun_wg0 device, Add, then open
    the created OPTx interface.
 9. Enable; Description: WG@CFG@. IPv4 Configuration Type: Static IPv4;
    IPv4 Address: @ADDR_IP@ / 24 (the tunnel network mask, so a gateway can
    live on it). MTU: @MTU@. Save, Apply Changes.
E. Gateway and static routes - the part config.xml MUST own
10. System > Routing > Gateways > Add: Interface WG@CFG@, Address Family
